{
  "dom_id": "step-q154829",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The interval $y\\in [-16,\\infty )$ corresponds to the inequality",
  "worked_solution": "The statement $y\\in [-16,\\infty )$ means that $y$ lies between $-16$ and $\\infty ,$ where \n\n- the left endpoint $-16$ *is* included, and\n\n- the right endpoint $\\infty $ is *not* included.\n\nTherefore, the inequality represented by this interval is \n\n$$\n-16\\le y<\\infty .\n$$\n\nHowever, since all numbers are smaller than infinity, it suffices to write \n\n$$\n-16\\le y\n$$\n\nor, equivalently, \n\n$$\ny\\ge -16.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
